# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# pnpm 12 reads its install settings from pnpm-workspace.yaml and ignores them
# here, so this file sets none. It stays for what pnpm still reads from
# .npmrc (registry and auth entries): pr.yml's path filters name it, and
# scripts/tests/test_pnpm_effective_policy.py fails on a setting here that pnpm
# ignores.
#
# The supply-chain policy (C-12.3) is in pnpm-workspace.yaml: ignoreScripts,
# frozenLockfile, saveExact and strictPeerDependencies, each with its reason.
# engine-strict, which this file used to set, is not carried over (the reason
# is there too).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# E02-T07: the root package's own `prepare` script (`husky`) installs the git
# hooks under .husky/. `pnpm install` runs no lifecycle script (ignoreScripts),
# so contributors and CI run it explicitly, once per clone or worktree
# (reviewed in E02-X01):
#   pnpm run prepare
# It is a single, code-owned, checked-in script (`husky`, which only writes a
# `core.hooksPath` pointer and copies the committed `.husky/*` files: no
# network fetch, no arbitrary code execution). This is documented in
# CONTRIBUTING.md's setup steps. No other package may rely on
# `prepare`/`postinstall` without the same review + allowlist entry.
